from pathlib import Path
import json
from urllib.parse import quote
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;repo=B.parents[2];reports=repo/'astrdocs';D=B.parents[3]
read=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
summary=read(B/'delivery-summary.json');courses=read(B/'courses.json');checks=read(B/'checks.json');browser=read(B/'browser-checks.json');verification=read(B/'original-verification.json')
old=read(reports/'all-50-delivery.json');projects=old['projects']+summary
total=lambda key:sum(r[key] for r in projects)
batch=lambda key:sum(r[key] for r in summary)
count=lambda kind:sum(r['check']==kind for r in checks)
course=lambda name:quote('../../'+name+'/astraupskill/README.md',safe='/+')
lines=['# Next 25 projects: implementation report','','Completed September 8, 2026. This batch adds projects 51–75 to the previous 50, focusing on compact CRUD learning projects and bounded improvements to the larger teaching scaffolds. The changes are applied in each original Desktop folder, including the selected project in `_Organized Desktop`.','','## What was delivered','',f'- **25 project improvements**, with {batch("changes")} changed or new files.',f'- **225 learning documents**, nine per project, totaling {batch("learning_words"):,} words.',f'- **{batch("test_cases")} passing test cases**, {count("build")} client builds and {count("server-build")} server builds.',f'- **{sum("typecheck" in r["check"] for r in checks)} passing TypeScript checks**, 14 migration commands, 14 seed commands and 25 Chromium interaction checks.','','The courses teach a junior SWE how to read the actual code, trace a request, validate input, preserve data integrity, test failures, debug and implement a related improvement independently. Optional exercises are clearly separated from delivered changes.','','## Suggested learning order','','Start with 51 and 58–61 for validation, edit forms and CRUD request flow. Continue with 52–56 and 72 for persistence, ownership and transactions. Study 62–66 for membership, capacity, checkout and booking races. Move to 67–71 for archive/restore and bulk audit consistency, then 57 for WebSockets and 73–75 for backup validation and authenticated application tracking.','','| # | Project and course | Implemented improvement | Tests |','|---|---|---|---:|']
for r,c in zip(summary,courses):lines.append(f'| {r["stage"]} | [{r["project"]}]({course(r["project"])}) | {c["after"].replace("|","/")} | {r["test_cases"]} |')
lines+=['','## Learning folder in every project','','`astraupskill/` contains:','','1. `README.md` — setup, goals and course sequence.','2. `01-CODEBASE-MAP.md` — files, responsibilities and reading order.','3. `02-CONCEPTS.md` — concepts explained from first principles.','4. `03-WORKED-CHANGE.md` — actual source excerpts and executable examples.','5. `04-TESTING-AND-DEBUGGING.md` — regressions, failure cases and diagnosis.','6. `05-PRACTICE.md` — guided and independent exercises.','7. `06-SOLUTIONS-AND-REVIEW.md` — solutions, tradeoffs and review criteria.','8. `07-TRACE-LAB.md` — detailed request/state traces and checkpoints.','9. `VERIFICATION.md` — checks performed, reproduction instructions and limits.','','## Verification scope','','Checks used isolated working copies, disposable PostgreSQL schemas, temporary SQLite storage or fresh browser storage. The browser harness forwarded requests to actual local servers and adjusted CORS for its temporary origin. The original databases and dependency installations were not replaced. The two browser-storage projects used their own declared dependency installations; other checks used recorded verification-workspace dependencies. A clean install in every original folder and deployed integrations are not claimed.','','The implementation includes repaired JSON seed serialization, database CLI scripts, compiled server entry paths, stable auth selectors and React module deduplication where needed. One support-ticket seed referenced a nonexistent `subject` column; it now uses the actual `title` column.','','A 390px screenshot and document-width measurement were captured for every project. See each verification page for its measured result; this is not a full responsive or accessibility audit.','','## Boundaries and next work','']
for c,r in zip(courses,summary):lines.append(f'- **{r["project"]}:** {c["limitations"]}')
lines+=['','## Delivery evidence','',f'After application, all **{verification["files_checked"]:,} delivered files across 75 projects** matched their expected hashes. All 675 course files and {verification["local_links_checked"]:,} local course links were checked. Earlier projects were checked for delivery integrity; their historical test suites were not rerun in this batch.','','[Manifest](../astrafinalplan/implementation/batch04/delivery-manifest.json) · [Checks](../astrafinalplan/implementation/batch04/checks.json) · [Browser results](../astrafinalplan/implementation/batch04/browser-checks.json) · [Source diff](../astrafinalplan/implementation/batch04/source-changes.diff) · [Dependency versions](../astrafinalplan/implementation/batch04/dependency-versions.json) · [Original-file verification](../astrafinalplan/implementation/batch04/original-verification.json)','','Original versions of changed files are retained in `astrafinalplan/implementation/batch04/backups/`. Project 75 has unrelated nested projects; those were excluded from this delivery.','']
(reports/'NEXT_25_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8')
allrows=['# All 75 projects: delivered improvements and learning courses','',f'As of September 8, 2026: **75 projects, {total("learning_files")} learning files, {total("learning_words"):,} learning words, and {total("test_cases")} test cases recorded across the four batches.**','','The latest batch contributes 25 projects and 225 documents. [Latest detailed report](NEXT_25_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md) · [Previous 50-project report](ALL_50_PROJECTS_REPORT.md)','','The sequence below preserves the delivery order. For a CRUD learning path through the latest batch, follow the suggested order in its report.','','| # | Original project and course | Learning files | Tests |','|---|---|---:|---:|']
for r in projects:allrows.append(f'| {int(r["stage"])} | [{r["project"]}]({course(r["project"])}) | {r["learning_files"]} | {r["test_cases"]} |')
allrows+=['',f'Delivery verification: {verification["files_checked"]:,} files checked; no hash mismatches. Tests from earlier batches retain their historical verification dates. The latest batch checks and limitations are documented per project.','']
(reports/'ALL_75_PROJECTS_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(allrows),encoding='utf-8')
(reports/'all-75-delivery.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(completed='2026-09-08',projects=projects,latest_batch_checks=checks,latest_browser_checks=browser,original_verification=verification),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
(reports/'SUMMARY.md').write_text(f'''# Concise delivery summary

**75 projects now have implemented improvements and detailed junior SWE courses.** The latest 25 focus on CRUD web development.

- **Code:** validated inputs, reliable editing, ownership checks, transaction boundaries, archive/restore, bulk updates, backup imports and repaired setup commands.
- **Learning:** nine files per project; **675 total**, including **225 new documents** with explanations, examples, exercises, solutions and debugging labs.
- **Latest checks:** **{batch('test_cases')} tests, 25 client builds, 14 server builds, 28 database setup commands and 25 browser checks passed.** Delivery hashes and course links were checked across all 75 projects.
- **Start here:** Legal Case Tracker, then Blog Platform, Kanban Board, Job Application Tracker and Inventory Management. Follow with the transaction and database projects.

[All projects and course links](ALL_75_PROJECTS_REPORT.md) · [Latest 25 changes](NEXT_25_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md)
''',encoding='utf-8')
for folder in [reports,repo/'astradocs',repo/'astrafinalplan']:
 p=folder/'README.md'
 if p.exists():
  link='ALL_75_PROJECTS_REPORT.md' if folder==reports else '../astrdocs/ALL_75_PROJECTS_REPORT.md'
  entry=f'\n## Latest implementation: 75 projects\n\n[All 75 projects and learning courses]({link}). The latest 25 CRUD-focused improvements are applied to their original folders, with nine detailed learning files each.\n'
  text=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
  if '## Latest implementation: 75 projects' not in text:p.write_text(text.rstrip()+'\n'+entry,encoding='utf-8')
print(json.dumps(dict(projects=75,learning_files=total('learning_files'),learning_words=total('learning_words'),tests=total('test_cases'),latest_tests=batch('test_cases')),indent=2))
